# guests.registry — the guests known to this benchmark. Single source of truth for the
# root tools (gen-witness · gen-elf · execute), parsed via reg.sh. One row per guest,
# `|`-separated (surrounding spaces ignored). Add a guest = add a row.
#
#   name | infra_dir | run_guest | eth_var | vendor_dir | elf | witness | exec | description
#
# elf     : build (from vendor_dir) · presupplied (shipped in-repo) ·
#           record (guests/<name>/build.sh, driven by guests/<name>/<name>.build) ·
#           monad  (cli/build-monad -> the monad tree's own zkvm/zisk/build-official.sh)
# witness : rpc (standard archive RPC) · rpc-debug (needs a debug_executionWitness node) ·
#           presupplied (shipped in-repo) · toy (not a block witness)
# exec    : input (./run execute ELF INPUT) · block (./run execute BLOCK) · batch (guests/monad/ev.sh)
#
rsp        | infra/sp1-infra    | rsp         | RSP_DIR        | vendor/rsp             | build       | rpc         | input | SP1 · reth (RSP)
openvm     | infra/openvm-infra | openvm-reth | OPENVM_ETH_DIR | vendor/openvm-eth      | build       | rpc         | block | OpenVM · reth
zisk       | infra/zisk-infra   | zisk-reth   | ZISK_ETH_DIR   | vendor/zisk-eth-client | build       | rpc-debug   | input | ZisK · reth
# monad: guest program presupplied in guests/monad/. `exec=batch` = EXECUTE+verify via guests/monad/ev.sh.
# Both variants are ALSO PROVABLE via cli/prove-farm: each routes to its stack (run_guest=monad-<zkvm> →
# guests/monad-<zkvm>/{monad-<zkvm>.elf, inputs/<tag>.bin}, built by that dir's gen-inputs). The inputs
# differ per zkVM: ZisK wants the ziskos length-prefixed format; SP1's runner takes the raw witness
# (it write_slice()s the file as one opaque buffer).
monad-sp1  | infra/sp1-infra    | monad-sp1   | -              | -                      | presupplied | presupplied | batch | Monad guest on SP1
monad-zisk | infra/zisk-infra   | monad-zisk  | -              | -                      | presupplied | presupplied | batch | Monad guest on ZisK
fibonacci  | infra/sp1-infra    | fibonacci   | -              | -                      | build       | toy         | input | SP1 example guest
# The two sides of the ZisK headline comparison. Neither builds the way the reth guests do, and
# they do not build the same way as each other: ziskethone is a C++ cmake guest behind an upstream
# driver, pinned by a hand-written <name>.build record; a Monad guest is built by the monad tree's
# own fail-closed recipe, and its <name>.build.json is written by that recipe's auditor. Add
# another Monad build with `cli/build-monad --name <n> --branch <b>` plus a row here.
ziskethone      | infra/zisk-infra | ziskethone      | - | vendor/zisk-eth-client | record | rpc-debug    | input | ZisK · ziskethone (upstream C++ reference)
monad-r10-zisk  | infra/zisk-infra | monad-r10-zisk  | - | -                      | monad  | presupplied  | input | Monad guest, al/zkvm-r10 (input must be ziskos-framed)
